{"chunk_id": "78be9c4d02ee", "text": "Kaikeyi reveals to Bharata that she demanded two boons from King Dasharatha: the exile of Rama and the installation of Bharata as heir. The king obeyed his promise but died of grief after Rama departed with Sita and Lakshmana. Rather than rejoice, Bharata is devastated and furious. He condemns his mother\u2019s ambition, accusing her of destroying the king, shaming the Ikshvaku dynasty, and exiling the righteous Rama who loved her like a mother. Bharata insists the throne belongs by sacred custom to the eldest son and rejects the kingdom gained through injustice. Declaring he will never fulfill Kaikeyi\u2019s wishes, he vows to bring Rama back from the forest and serve him. The episode establishes Bharata\u2019s moral greatness and loyalty, reinforcing the epic\u2019s central theme of dharma over power.\nBharata condemns Kaikeyi for Rama\u2019s exile and Dasaratha\u2019s death, rejects the throne, and vows to bring Rama back and serve him.\nThemes: filial conflict, righteous kingship, loyalty to Rama, condemnation of greed, dynastic duty", "vector": [0.011098659597337246, -0.02153972163796425, -0.012031377293169498, -0.006545793730765581, -0.01354117039591074, 0.021996013820171356, -0.03347044438123703, -0.013715635053813457, -0.016882846131920815, -0.008797063492238522, 0.017862534150481224, 0.00701215211302042, 0.005495648365467787, 0.024774033576250076, -0.020908962935209274, 0.012205841951072216, 0.040502727031707764, -0.009635837748646736, 0.031027935445308685, -0.010011608712375164, -0.005233950912952423, -0.008173015899956226, -0.004019405692815781, 0.020761338993906975, -0.025928188115358353, 0.00860246829688549, 0.013702214695513248, -0.038677554577589035, 0.019741389900445938, -0.014453756622970104, -0.012588323093950748, -0.0023468900471925735, 0.0009427822078578174, 0.003024619771167636, -0.029122238978743553, 0.01257490273565054, -0.018520133569836617, -0.0008857455104589462, 0.008495104499161243, 0.0053614447824656